A||N||1||Cplensdorf||Subwoofer Not Working!!!||||9||
Z||000000||Cplensdorf||07-22-2001||10:08 PM||||My factory subwoofer appears to be working. It is 'stuck' with full bass.  The 'performance' switch appears to make no difference.  Any ideas?<P>||||reg||9
Z||000001||kslish||07-22-2001||11:58 PM||||The subwoofer slider has to be grounded for it to work....otherwise the amp will run at full power like you are experiencing.  Probable causes could be: the slider has gone bad or has dirty contacts, the switch isn't grounded properly (it is grounded via a screw similar to the way the overhead console lights are grounded), or something is up with the wiring.<P>Just somethings to look at and/or test.  It could be something else entirely (like a bad amp), but these are the things I would check first.<P><BR>------------------<BR>Ken S.<BR>'87GT and '86SC<BR>See them at <A HREF="http://homepage.mac.com/kjslish/Fiero.html" TARGET=_blank>http://homepage.mac.com/kjslish/Fiero.html</A><BR>Western PA Fiero Club - <A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.westpennfiero.org</A><p>[This message has been edited by kslish (edited 07-23-2001).]||||reg||1
